<TR>
<TD class="left border-right-single">15. War Hazards Compensation</TD>
<TD class="left border-right-single">War Hazards Compensation Act, Act of Dec. 2, 1942, ch. 668, Title I, 56 Stat. 1028 42 U.S.C. 1701-1717</TD>
<TD class="left border-right-single">The War Hazards Compensation Act provides that certain provisions of the FECA and the LHWCA apply to certain persons employed by government contractors outside the continental United States who sustain an injury proximately caused by a war risk hazard. Sec. 101(c), 42 U.S.C. 1701(c), provides that compensation for disability or death to aliens and non-nationals of the United States who are not residents of the United States or Canada under the Act is in the same amount as residents, &#x201C;except that dependents in any foreign country shall be limited to surviving wife or husband and child or children.&#x201D;</TD>
